  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "TRIAL EDITION - SQL longer than 10,000 characters is rejected (parse() returns -1). Full edition: https://www.sqlparser.com\n\nRelease 4.1.0.12\n\n- [DB2] Accept the sqlstate of SIGNAL and RESIGNAL given as a CHAR(5)\n  variable rather than a string literal, for example\n  SIGNAL SQLSTATE VALUE P_STATE, with or without the VALUE keyword.\n  The variable may be qualified, as a parameter by the routine name or\n  a local by its block label, for example SIGNAL SQLSTATE P1.P_STATE.\n  A handler condition is unaffected and still requires a constant,\n  which is what DB2 specifies.\n  Known limitation: a variable named literally VALUE cannot be used in\n  this position, because SQLSTATE VALUE x would then be ambiguous with\n  the VALUE keyword. Variables named after other unreserved keywords,\n  such as RESULT or DATA, work normally.\n- [DB2] Accept a qualified condition name, both module.condition and\n  schema.module.condition, in a handler condition list and in SIGNAL\n  and RESIGNAL. The name in a condition declaration stays unqualified,\n  as DB2 requires.\n\nDemos: https://github.com/sqlparser/gsp_demo_dotnet",
